.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMO-LIST-ALERT-HISTORY 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emo-list-alert-history \- show the alert state changes, newest first
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli emo list-alert-history
[\fB\-\-rule\-id\fR|\fB\-r\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-from\fR \fITIME\fR]
[\fB\-\-to\fR \fITIME\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR|\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every change of state any rule of the account made, newest first: which
series, from what to what, the figure and the line that decided it, and
when. A change made because the rule itself changed carries a
.I reason
\-
.IR rule-deleted ,
.I rule-disabled
or
.I rule-changed
\- and is otherwise empty.
.PP
The same changes are published on the event bus as they happen. The bus
is delivery, and an event is gone once its subscribers have taken it;
this is the record. Each entry is kept for
.I euclid.modules.emo.alert.history-retention
days, 90 as shipped, and then removed by the database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule\-id " " \fIID\fR
Only this rule's changes.
.TP
.BR \-\-from " " \fITIME\fR
From this time, inclusive. ISO 8601, e.g.
.IR 2026-10-31T00:00:00Z .
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fITIME\fR
Until this time, exclusive.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR
How many. Default 100.
.SH OUTPUT
.RS
.nf
{"items": [{"ruleId": "system-cpu-per-host", "name": "system-cpu-usage",
            "labels": {"host": "vogje01-pios"}, "previous": "OK",
            "state": "WARNING", "severity": "warning", "value": 83.4,
            "threshold": 80, "statistic": "value", "reason": "",
            "timestamp": "2026-10-31T12:05:00Z", ...}]}
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The changes were printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated, or is not an administrator.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
# The last hundred changes
euclid-cli emo list-alert-history

# One rule, today
euclid-cli emo list-alert-history --rule-id system-cpu-per-host \\
    --from 2026-10-31T00:00:00Z
.fi
.RE
